      "content": "The problem is that a \"metadata layer\" doesn't solve the core issue. In the Solaris case, the opposition is going to use aggressive, non-standard litigation tactics that haven't been seen in precedent yet. A rule-based database is only going to tell us what has happened before; it won't help us anticipate what they might do next. If we switch to that system now, we're essentially flying blind on the predictive side. Are you saying the transition team can actually manage those high-stakes files with just historical context and no active strategic intelligence?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
